  m_text: 'At memorial services, a choir can give a community a shared voice. Hymns
    and choral music connect the words of a service with familiar rituals of gathering,
    reflection and remembrance.


    For many people, singing together is part of
    how faith and community are practised: voices carry prayers, mark moments of
    silence, and offer comfort to those remembering loved ones. The sound can hold
    personal memories as well as public history.


    As you listen here, consider
    what this place means to the people who gather at the memorial, and how music
    helps a community remember.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
